// Title: Service Reconnaissance Via Wmic.EXE
// Sigma ID: 76f55eaa-d27f-4213-9d45-7b0e4b60bbae
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-14 | Modified: 2026-01-07
// ATT&CK: execution, T1047
// Description: An adversary might use WMI to check if a certain remote service is running on a remote device.
//   When the test completes, a service information will be displayed on the screen if it exists. A
//   common feedback message is that "No instance(s) Available" if the service queried is not
//   running. A common error message is "Node - (provided IP or default) ERROR Description =The RPC
//   server is unavailable" if the provided remote host is unreachable
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1047/T1047.md
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/wmic
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/cimwin32prov/win32-service
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wmic_recon_service.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\WMIC.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "service") and (not(((ProcessCommandLine contains "stopservice" or ProcessCommandLine contains "startservice") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "Change" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Create" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Delete" or ProcessCommandLine contains "PauseService" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ResumeService" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SetSecurityDescriptor" or ProcessCommandLine contains "StartService" or ProcessCommandLine contains "StopService" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UserControlService"))))
